# VISA Vulnerability Agentic Harness (VVAH) — Comprehensive Architectural Analysis

## 1. Project Identity & Purpose

**What it is:** VVAH is Visa's open-source agentic SAST (Static Application Security Testing) pipeline for autonomous vulnerability discovery, remediation, and validation, built on learnings from [Project Glasswing](https://www.anthropic.com/glasswing) (Anthropic's AI-assisted vulnerability research initiative).

**Problem domain:** Vulnerability triage for software security. The project explicitly addresses the bottleneck in AI-assisted vulnerability management: not discovery speed, but **Mean Time to Adapt (MTTA)** — elapsed time from AI-discovered exploitability to a validated fix in production. Key innovation: multi-agent deterministic voting + threat modeling + structured triage artifacts to compress triage lifecycle.

**Core files:**
- [README.md](README.md#L1-L70) — feature overview, 4-phase pipeline description
- [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md#L1-L40) — operating manual for AI agents
- [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md#L1-L100) — module layout and data flow diagram
