### 8.2 Shared Prompt Blocks

Reusable blocks in [vvaharness/util/prompts.py](vvaharness/util/prompts.py#L1-L100):

```python
EXCLUSION_RULES = """
OUT OF SCOPE — do not report:
A. NO REAL ATTACKER (tests, dev-only, local-only inputs)
B. NO SECURITY IMPACT (crashes, design-as-intended)
C. WRONG LAYER (client-side vs. server-side, managed languages)
D. HANDLED ELSEWHERE (SCA/dependencies, volumetric DoS)
E. NOISE FLOOR (log injection, LLM prompts, theoretical gaps)
"""

SELF_VERIFICATION = """
GATE EVERY FINDING ON THESE FIVE CHECKS:
1. REACHABLE
2. UNMITIGATED
3. CONCRETE
4. IN SCOPE
5. CITED
"""

SEVERITY_GUIDANCE = """..."""
EXHAUSTIVENESS = """..."""
```

Injected into S4, S6, S7, S8 prompts via `${BLOCK}` or direct concatenation.

### 8.3 Templating & Context Injection

**Context blocks assembled deterministically:**
```python
# ContextPackage.to_prompt_block() in models.py
def to_prompt_block(self, max_edges: int = 400) -> str:
    lines = [
        f"REPO: {self.repo_root}  LANG: {self.language}",
        "",
        f"MODULES ({len(self.modules)}):",
        # ... module details
        f"ALL FILES ({len(self.all_files)}):",
        # ... entry points, sinks, call graph, ...
    ]
    return "\n".join(lines)
```

**No Jinja2 / mustache templating.** All prompts are hardcoded Python strings with `.format()` or f-strings.

### 8.4 Prompt Caching

**Anthropic SDK backend only** ([backends/sdk.py](vvaharness/backends/sdk.py#L150-L200)):
```python
# S4 deep-dive runs the same system_prompt N times; cache it.
cache_control = {"type": "ephemeral"}  # Anthropic cache header
response = client.messages.create(
    model=model_id,
    system=[
        {"type": "text", "text": system_prompt},
        {"type": "text", "text": "...", "cache_control": cache_control},
    ],
    messages=[{"role": "user", "content": user_prompt}],
    ...
)
```
Cache hits for S4 repeated runs: ~10% cost savings.

